    "result_text": "Done. The change is green \u2014 full suite `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## What I added\n\nFollowing the existing `RequireUniqueTelephone` / `RequireUniqueHousehold` reject-rule pattern, I added three small new units plus one wiring edit \u2014 no existing function bodies changed, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **`RequireCityCapacity`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners whose city matches the request's city and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50. A single cohesive method with CC 2 and no surrounding class complexity (WMC_other = 0).\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (new checked exception) \u2014 mirrors `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (new escalation handler) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT`, plus its escalation YAML.\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `capacity` step (governed by `transaction`) between `household` and `build`, so an at-capacity city is rejected before the owner is built/saved.\n\nThe rule runs on the `POST /api/owners` pipeline; the 51st owner in a city that already holds 50 gets a 409.",
